# Build output. The binaries are large and rebuilt by `make build`; a committed
# one is also the fastest way to deploy a build nobody can reproduce.
bin/
dist/

# Coverage and profiling artefacts.
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.prof
*.test

# Secrets. `.env.example` is committed and documents every variable; `.env`
# holds the values and must never be.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local
*.pem
*.key
!testdata/**/*.pem

# Local database dumps and backup artefacts. A dump of a real database is the
# most sensitive file this project can produce.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
backups/
/tmp/

# What a deployment creates beside the compose file: the signing secret and the
# database password, the off-host audit copy, the WAL archive, and the local
# choices in .env. Ignored so that a server's own keys cannot be committed back
# by someone tidying up a working directory.
deploy/secrets/
deploy/audit-archive/
deploy/postgres/
deploy/.env

# Performance and load-test output, regenerated by `make perf`.
# Perf run artefacts (results and server logs), not the harness in cmd/perf.
/perf/

# Node output for the operator UI. The UI builds from source; node_modules is
# never committed.
node_modules/
web/dist/
npm-debug.log*

# The React interface's build output, regenerated by `make ui-build`.
#
# The directory itself is kept in the tree by a .gitkeep, and that is load
# bearing rather than habit: webui/embed.go embeds this directory, so a clone
# without it fails `go build` with an embed error that names no remedy. Keeping
# only the marker means the build output never dirties a working tree, and a
# binary built before `make ui-build` serves a page saying exactly that.
#
# The re-inclusion of the directory has to come first — git does not descend
# into an ignored directory, so a bare negation inside one is never reached.
!webui/dist/
webui/dist/*
!webui/dist/.gitkeep

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
